{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790732559,"nonce":"y41RuLHfJRjygEya6xHVIlwMKUU=","message":"Root cause isolated by ASH_PROFILE=all and --jit-log: with the default max_jit_args=8, 82.7% of sampled CPU was in the interpreter. Interpreted findex 812, 453, and 798 accounted for 38.7%, 30.7%, and 18.5% of interpreter samples. The promotion gate skipped them because their signatures have 16, 10, and 11 arguments; another reached function has 17. Lowering the tier-zero call threshold from 10 to 1 did not help. Increasing --jit-max-args to 32 lets the existing Cranelift AIR V2 and uniform-entry path compile them. With the same warm harness and no profiler, five-run serial medians fell from about 3.1 s (eight-argument Cranelift-only hybrid) to 258.8 ms (32-argument Cranelift-only hybrid); auto hybrid with 32 was 247.9 ms. Forced Cranelift JIT was about 243 ms in a control run. State parity passed. Host contention later made absolute timings vary, but explicit 32 and the new default behaved alike. A 16-argument closure-call regression fixture covers the default path. The separate LLVM queue policy opportunity is tracked in cb93154605be6d0d8bea8f1faefaba9022983bb9ca498df6cf2fc4d01a74558e.","files":null}]}